scored tokens: ". Emily Chen had always known that she wanted to be a doctor. As a child, she was fascinated by the human body and its intricate workings, and as she grew older, her passion for medicine only intensified. She spent countless hours studying, volunteering at hospitals, and shadowing doctors, determined to turn her dream into a reality.\n\nAfter years of hard work, Dr. Chen finally graduated from medical school with top honors. She landed a residency at one of the most prestigious hospitals in the city, where she quickly made a name for herself as a talented and compassionate physician.\n\nDr. Chen's days were long and demanding, but she loved every minute of it. She spent her mornings seeing patients in the clinic, diagnosing illnesses and prescribing treatments. In the afternoons, she was on call in the emergency room, treating everything from broken bones to life-threatening emergencies.\n\nDespite the stress and pressure of her job, Dr. Chen never lost sight of what mattered most: her patients. She took the time to listen to their concerns, answer their questions, and offer words of comfort and encouragement. She knew that sometimes, the best medicine was simply a kind word or a gentle touch.\n\nOne day, Dr. Chen was called to the ER to see a young boy who<|im_end|>\n"
